{"duration_api_ms":309175,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"37aef69c-4a46-423c-a2bc-f41b5ff2f50d","total_cost_usd":0.34160399999999996,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12400,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":29200,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":22478},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12400,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":29200,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12400,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12400},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":29200,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12400,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.34160399999999996,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":22478,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"Only 2 of 20 evaluated designs are feasible, and only C-ca305253716b is non-dominated (flux 345120 W/m2, Tbond 406.56 K). Eleven of the 20 failed on geometry, so the hypervolume is mostly limited by wasted slots and by the max_g limit (12 g), which caps how steep the entry angle can be. I backed out the constraint limits from the margins: max_g 12, bondline 450 K, and heatshield mass fraction roughly 0.09*D^2 relative to its limit, so D is capped near 3.3 m. The geometry failures are consistent with nose radius = bluntness*D and shoulder radius = 0.1*D. Fore-cone length is then proportional to 0.4 - (b-0.1)*cos(theta), so a design is valid only if (b-0.1)*cos(theta) < 0.4. The formula reproduces the reported negative lengths for C-892b8b20e709 and C-c170e00795a8. I keep it below about 0.38 in every proposal. Bluntness above 0.9 needs a cone half-angle of 60 deg or more.\",\"evidence\":[\"Geometry: C-c170e00795a8 (b=0.929, 53.06 deg gives 0.4985), C-892b8b20e709 (0.608) and C-77238b231f4a fail. C-ca305253716b (0.367), C-30ab3c9fdbef (0.362) and C-f1dfaff79f31 (0.246) are valid, consistent with a 0.4 threshold.\",\"max_g: 9.85 at gamma=-2.32 (C-30ab3c9fdbef), 11.20 at -3.16 (C-ca305253716b), 13.57 at -4.54 (C-7e930f570744). This fits g ~ 6.1 + 1.63*|gamma| for large D, so the g limit of 12 allows |gamma| up to about 3.6 deg. Small-D designs (C-7139ecfe995b, C-6c8d751b6b54) run 1-1.5 g higher.\",\"Mass fraction: margins of 0.185 (D=3.007), 0.171 (D=3.044), 0.452 (D=2.48), -0.37 (D=3.74) and -0.77 (D=4.33) scale as D^2. Zero margin falls near D~3.3-3.35 m.\",\"Scaling fitted to the rows: flux falls with D and with nose radius, and rises only weakly with |gamma| (C-7e930f570744 vs C-ca305253716b, C-1d847642b793). Bondline temperature (T-300) scales roughly as D^-0.5 * sin(gamma)^-0.35 with almost no dependence on nose radius, so steeper entry lowers T (C-1d847642b793 372 K, C-0a0993b4b67b 374 K). Larger bluntness at high cone angle therefore lowers flux without raising T.\",\"Small-D designs (C-6c8d751b6b54: 2.63e6 W/m2, 510 K; C-7139ecfe995b) are far worse on both objectives and infeasible, so the useful region is D ~3.0-3.35 m, gamma ~ -3.3 to -3.6 deg, with high bluntness and cone angle.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Bigger diameter lowers ballistic coefficient, so peak density and heat load fall. A larger nose radius (bluntness*D) cuts stagnation-point flux roughly as 1/sqrt(Rn). Steeper entry shortens the heating pulse and lowers the integrated load that drives bondline temperature, but raises peak deceleration, which max_g caps near gamma ~ -3.6 deg. Large cone angle raises drag and gives room for high bluntness within the geometry limit. Heatshield mass fraction grows with D^2 and is the binding constraint at the large-D end. Tbond has the larger effect on hypervolume, since each 10 K is worth about 0.067 of the normalised T axis, so I push toward the steepest gamma that keeps g under 12, the largest allowed D, and high bluntness. Some proposals probe the g and mass-fraction boundaries and single-variable effects (bluntness, cone angle, gamma) to calibrate the model.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The scaling exponents and the g and mass-fraction fits come from 9 valid points, so the numeric predictions are rough (about +/-10% on flux, +/-5 K on T). Geometry validity assumes Rn=b*D and Rs=0.1*D, fitted to two failure lengths, and there may be other minimum-length rules. I do not know how cone angle enters drag, g or mass fraction, and proposals at D>=3.3 or gamma <= -3.55 may fail max_g or mass fraction.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Enlarge the feasible best design (D 3.007 -> 3.25) and steepen gamma to -3.4. Expect lower flux and T while g (~11.6) and mass fraction (~0.95 of limit) stay inside limits.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.25,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":312000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Most conservative step that should dominate the current front point; calibrates the D and gamma exponents.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Same as the previous D=3.25 proposal but at gamma=-3.55, close to the g limit, to see how much T falls with steeper entry.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.25,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":314000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":398.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the g boundary near gamma=-3.55 (predicted ~11.9 g) with a large-D design.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Increase D to 3.3, bluntness to 0.9 and cone angle to 64 deg. Larger nose radius should cut flux, and the geometry term is 0.351, so it is valid.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.9,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":64.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":287000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether blunter, larger designs push flux well below 300k with T near 400 K; mass fraction is close to its limit (~0.98).\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"High bluntness (1.15) with the maximum cone angle (70 deg), where the geometry term is 0.359, to get a very large nose radius (3.8 m) and low flux.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.15,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":255000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Probes the low-flux corner of the design space; extends the front toward flux < 300k.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-7e930f570744\",\"rationale\":\"Take the 66.6 deg design that failed only on g (13.57), reduce |gamma| to -3.5 (about 11.8 g), and enlarge D to 3.25 with bluntness 0.75. The geometry term is 0.24.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.25,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.75,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":325000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Converts a near-feasible point into a feasible one and tests a moderate-bluntness, high-cone-angle region.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.2, bluntness 1.0, cone 67 deg (geometry term 0.352), gamma=-3.3. A mid-way point between conservative and aggressive designs.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":67.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":285000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":400.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds coverage of the trade-off front with a comfortably valid geometry and mass-fraction margin.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.25, bluntness 1.0, cone 68 deg, gamma=-3.5. Combines the large nose radius with steep entry.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.25,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":282000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Candidate to dominate the current point on both objectives.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Low cone angle (45 deg), low bluntness (0.5), D=3.0, geometry term 0.283. Checks how cone angle affects drag, flux, T, g and mass fraction.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.5,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":45.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":480000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":412.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Explores the other side of the cone-angle range to learn the sign and size of the cone-angle effect.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Boundary probe: D=3.35, bluntness 1.1, cone 70 deg. The D^2 mass-fraction estimate is ~0.99 of the limit, and the flat cone should keep mass low.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.35,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":255000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the upper D limit set by heatshield mass fraction; the result is informative whether it passes or fails.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-30ab3c9fdbef\",\"rationale\":\"Move the shallow feasible point C-30ab3c9fdbef to D=3.1 and gamma=-3.5, keeping bluntness 0.878 and cone 62.3 deg (already valid).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.1,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":323000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":400.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Uses a different parent geometry and the same valid bluntness/cone pair, adding diversity at low risk.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.2, bluntness 1.2, cone 70 deg (geometry term 0.376, valid by my fit but with a thin margin). Very large nose radius (3.84 m) at gamma=-3.5.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":263000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the extreme-bluntness corner, and also tests the geometry threshold at 0.376.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.3, bluntness 1.2, cone 70 deg, gamma=-3.6. This is the aggressive corner (near the g limit and the mass-fraction limit) that should give the lowest flux and T if it passes.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":253000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the combined limit of g (~11.97) and mass fraction; the result would define the corner of the feasible front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.15, bluntness 0.95, cone 66 deg (geometry term 0.346), gamma=-3.45. An interior point between the conservative and aggressive proposals.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.15,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.95,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":66.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.45},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":302000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":400.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills in the trade-off front between flux ~285k and ~345k.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-7e930f570744\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.2, bluntness 0.7, cone 69 deg, gamma=-3.5 from the C-7e930f570744 family (geometry term 0.215). Moderate nose radius.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.7,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":345000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":400.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether flux really depends on nose radius while T does not, by comparing with the high-bluntness proposals.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Keep D=3.007 and gamma=-3.16 changes minimal: raise bluntness to 1.1 and cone angle to 70 deg, and steepen gamma to -3.5. This isolates the bluntness/cone effect at D fixed.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":302000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":401.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Mass fraction is unchanged at D=3.007, so this is a safe probe of the bluntness and cone-angle benefit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Single-variable change: gamma from -3.157 to -3.5 with everything else fixed. Measures dT/dgamma, dflux/dgamma and g accurately.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":352000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":402.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Clean calibration of the gamma sensitivities, which the whole strategy depends on.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Single-variable change: cone half-angle from 58.8 to 68 deg (geometry term 0.265) to isolate the cone-angle effect on drag, flux, T and g.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":335000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":404.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"The cone-angle effect on the objectives is unknown; this is a clean measurement.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Single-variable change: bluntness from 0.808 to 0.6 (geometry term 0.259) to measure the bluntness effect on flux vs T.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":0.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":400000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":408.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks the fitted result that nose radius mainly affects flux and barely affects T.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-30ab3c9fdbef\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.25 with the valid 0.878/62.3 deg pair at gamma=-3.5. Alternative moderate-bluntness large-D design.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.25,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":301000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":398.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Another large-D, steep-entry point, with a different bluntness and cone-angle pair from the others.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.3, bluntness 1.05, cone 69 deg (geometry term 0.34), gamma=-3.5. My best-guess design on both objectives, kept slightly off the extreme corners to limit failure risk.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.05,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":269000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Likely the largest hypervolume gain per evaluation; worth a higher-fidelity check if it passes.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1}]}","ttft_ms":249906,"type":"result","duration_ms":309213,"uuid":"5e5d5c10-51c4-48d5-b98c-67c2f467a171","ttft_stream_ms":1530,"time_to_request_ms":36,"first_content_frame_ms":1530,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
